# Print-image report fixtures (docs/text_design.md §9). These are page images,
# not text in the usual sense: column alignment depends on exact byte positions,
# trailing spaces are significant padding, and form feeds (0x0C) are the page
# markers. Any normalization silently changes what the file MEANS, so all of it
# is disabled here rather than relied upon not to happen.
#
#   -text        no line-ending conversion in either direction
#   -whitespace  trailing space is data; do not flag it as an error
examples/fixtures/ari/*.rpt -text -whitespace
